(1600278, 214954, 4281, '<td valign="top">Canon doesn''t refer to its products as mk I unless they have been replaced by mk II already and the old product would therefor never be marked as mk I. ;)<br/> <br/>Anyway, as for the image I like it! It is creative, funny and well done. The main fault I see is the shadow off the hand and the ''device'' the the right. It would have been nice to have a light to the right as well in order to minimize shadows.</td>', 'Canon doesn''t refer to its products as mk I unless they have been replaced by mk II already and the old product would therefor never be marked as mk I. ;) Anyway, as for the image I like it! It is creative, funny and well done. The main fault I see is the shadow off the hand and the ''device'' the the right. It would have been nice to have a light to the right as well in order to minimize shadows.', '2005-08-10 08:23:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(1600279, 213928, 4281, '<td valign="top">I don''t really get it. The red color is meant to represent blood I guess, and you are trying to show the similarity and yet difference between real war (as an entertainment?) and fake war in movies.<br/>I don''t find the red color on the DVD cover to be that effective and what is the purpose of the pen and the knife? (Are you perhaps referring to the saying that the pen is mightier than the sword?)<br/>Anyway, I don''t find this to be an effective enough picture. It''s neither obvious enough or subtle enough in my opinion.<br/> <br/>I don''t like seeing the holster for the knife and you should have kept the background further back in order to make less light fall on it so it would be darker and one wouldn''t see the folding in it.</td>', 'I don''t really get it. The red color is meant to represent blood I guess, and you are trying to show the similarity and yet difference between real war (as an entertainment?) and fake war in movies.I don''t find the red color on the DVD cover to be that effective and what is the purpose of the pen and the knife? (Are you perhaps referring to the saying that the pen is mightier than the sword?)Anyway, I don''t find this to be an effective enough picture. It''s neither obvious enough or subtle enough in my opinion. I don''t like seeing the holster for the knife and you should have kept the background further back in order to make less light fall on it so it would be darker and one wouldn''t see the folding in it.', '2005-08-10 08:24:04.000000', NULL, 1),
