(1606731, 214032, 37893, '<td valign="top">I dig the look of concentration here. The thumb is pulled enough far away from the lens that this trick is pulled off :) Great expressions and lighting. <br/> <br/>Be vewy vewy quiet Chris :) Bumping to 8.</td>', 'I dig the look of concentration here. The thumb is pulled enough far away from the lens that this trick is pulled off :) Great expressions and lighting.  Be vewy vewy quiet Chris :) Bumping to 8.', '2005-08-12 18:11:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1606732, 214299, 37893, '<td valign="top">Great take on an old concept. I like the DOF and the clarity of the image. Bumping to 8.</td>', 'Great take on an old concept. I like the DOF and the clarity of the image. Bumping to 8.', '2005-08-12 18:11:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1606733, 214534, 9906, '<td valign="top">IMHO you have too many ellements in the shot making it look a little cluttered.  I think just the two figures on the stairs and one other thing would make this a more potent entrie...<br/>TC</td>', 'IMHO you have too many ellements in the shot making it look a little cluttered.  I think just the two figures on the stairs and one other thing would make this a more potent entrie...TC', '2005-08-12 18:11:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1606735, 213689, 37893, '<td valign="top">This is cool. I can almost see the excitement in your sons face :) Don''t drop the baby! I really like this photo. Bumping from 7 to 10.</td>', 'This is cool. I can almost see the excitement in your sons face :) Don''t drop the baby! I really like this photo. Bumping from 7 to 10.', '2005-08-12 18:13:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(1606736, 215171, 9906, '<td valign="top">Besides making my stomach twinge, this shot needs a bit of work.  First off, your lighting is a bit unimaginative.  Ya need some fill light coming from frame left.  Also the drop cloth in the back is a little wrinkled if ya didn''t notice.  ;-)  Your colors are what bother me the most though.  They are very dull.  Maybe play with the levels a little more to pull the color out of the image...<br/>TC</td>', 'Besides making my stomach twinge, this shot needs a bit of work.  First off, your lighting is a bit unimaginative.  Ya need some fill light coming from frame left.  Also the drop cloth in the back is a little wrinkled if ya didn''t notice.  ;-)  Your colors are what bother me the most though.  They are very dull.  Maybe play with the levels a little more to pull the color out of the image...TC', '2005-08-12 18:13:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(1606737, 214616, 9906, '<td valign="top">I really like this a lot!  You put a lot of effort into the set up for it.  Only thing I would change would be to make absolutely sure your toothpicks are perfect and maybe clone out the little spots in your background (two to the right of the frame catch my eye right away!) since it''s a members challenge...<br/>TC</td>', 'I really like this a lot!  You put a lot of effort into the set up for it.  Only thing I would change would be to make absolutely sure your toothpicks are perfect and maybe clone out the little spots in your background (two to the right of the frame catch my eye right away!) since it''s a members challenge...TC', '2005-08-12 18:17:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(1606740, 214468, 9906, '<td valign="top">A nice illusion.  I wanna know how it''s done.  However, it''s not too interesting of a shot overall.  I don''t have any ideas though how to make it have more pop...<br/>TC</td>', 'A nice illusion.  I wanna know how it''s done.  However, it''s not too interesting of a shot overall.  I don''t have any ideas though how to make it have more pop...TC', '2005-08-12 18:18:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(1606741, 214927, 14603, '<td valign="top">Simple idea but very effectively presented.<br/>Good luck.</td>', 'Simple idea but very effectively presented.Good luck.', '2005-08-12 18:19:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(1606743, 214880, 9906, '<td valign="top">Whenever I see a set up shot like this, I immediately look for the flaws.  After all with a shot like this you have total controll over all elements.  The first thing I notice here is that your lighting causes a reflection on the scales glass that dulls out the numbers.  Move things around a bit till the relection is gone and you got one hell of a shot.  I would also have put the headphone cord all on the scale''s pad as it looks awkward and conflicts with the scales ''reading'' the way ya got it here...<br/>TC</td>', 'Whenever I see a set up shot like this, I immediately look for the flaws.  After all with a shot like this you have total controll over all elements.  The first thing I notice here is that your lighting causes a reflection on the scales glass that dulls out the numbers.  Move things around a bit till the relection is gone and you got one hell of a shot.  I would also have put the headphone cord all on the scale''s pad as it looks awkward and conflicts with the scales ''reading'' the way ya got it here...TC', '2005-08-12 18:21:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(1606748, 214985, 9906, '<td valign="top">It''s a striking image but I don''t see an illusion...  It almosts violates the rules though as it''s almost entirely a photograph of another piece of work.<br/>TC</td>', 'It''s a striking image but I don''t see an illusion...  It almosts violates the rules though as it''s almost entirely a photograph of another piece of work.TC', '2005-08-12 18:22:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(1606749, 214456, 9906, '<td valign="top">Too small and too much going on.  I almost didn''t even see the little girl diving into the box.  You would have had a great shot if ya cleared away all but the cookie box in question on both shelves and had only the top shelf at the top of frame, the girl going into a much bigger box and nothing else.  Remember simpler is almost always better.  Especially true in set up shots!<br/>TC</td>', 'Too small and too much going on.  I almost didn''t even see the little girl diving into the box.  You would have had a great shot if ya cleared away all but the cookie box in question on both shelves and had only the top shelf at the top of frame, the girl going into a much bigger box and nothing else.  Remember simpler is almost always better.  Especially true in set up shots!TC', '2005-08-12 18:24:56.000000', NULL, 1),
