(1611608, 215112, 39610, '<td valign="top">Thank you all for your great comments.<br/>I searched the internet for photo illusions and tricks and found this page <a href="//www.flickr.com/photos/w00kie/sets/180637/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.flickr.com/photos/w00kie/sets/180637/</a> <br/>So I began with taking a photo of this setup with the hand using my brother as a model. Do not wear any long sleeves since it makes part 2 more difficult. Then I uploaded the image into the laptop, put the laptop in place and adjusted the image through the viewfinder of the camera to find out if things matched. Then my brother put on a shirt with long sleeve and took care not to show any part of the hand. I adjusted the hand according to the perspective of the viewfinder and "click".<br/>It is necessary to put the camera on a tripod or somewhere where it is stable and won''t move.<br/>I was not happy about lot of things i.e. the position of the laptop image is to low, the lighting is terrible (500W handheld halogen right above scene), image not very sharp and the composition isnt that great but it got me no. 7 so me happy ;-)<br/>This takes some practice but I dare you all to try because the final product looks great as desktop wallpaper and family, friends and/or coworkers will scratch their heads till they become bald trying to figure this one out.</td>', 'Thank you all for your great comments.I searched the internet for photo illusions and tricks and found this page //www.flickr.com/photos/w00kie/sets/180637/ So I began with taking a photo of this setup with the hand using my brother as a model. Do not wear any long sleeves since it makes part 2 more difficult. Then I uploaded the image into the laptop, put the laptop in place and adjusted the image through the viewfinder of the camera to find out if things matched. Then my brother put on a shirt with long sleeve and took care not to show any part of the hand. I adjusted the hand according to the perspective of the viewfinder and "click".It is necessary to put the camera on a tripod or somewhere where it is stable and won''t move.I was not happy about lot of things i.e. the position of the laptop image is to low, the lighting is terrible (500W handheld halogen right above scene), image not very sharp and the composition isnt that great but it got me no. 7 so me happy ;-)This takes some practice but I dare you all to try because the final product looks great as desktop wallpaper and family, friends and/or coworkers will scratch their heads till they become bald trying to figure this one out.', '2005-08-15 06:57:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(1611613, 214829, 21714, '<td valign="top">Well done, Les. You keep getting better and better.</td>', 'Well done, Les. You keep getting better and better.', '2005-08-15 07:20:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(1611616, 213900, 32754, '<td valign="top">Thank you for comments and votes, even the 1, haha...this was my second picture with a greater than 6 average, and I am happy about it..sorry if this image disturbed a lot of people, but I had just seen a movie about Jimmy Hoffa and began thinking about him possibly being buried in cement somewhere and what being trapped in cement might look like...</td>', 'Thank you for comments and votes, even the 1, haha...this was my second picture with a greater than 6 average, and I am happy about it..sorry if this image disturbed a lot of people, but I had just seen a movie about Jimmy Hoffa and began thinking about him possibly being buried in cement somewhere and what being trapped in cement might look like...', '2005-08-15 07:31:05.000000', NULL, 0),
