(1611914, 215207, 30817, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by graphicfunk:</b></div><hr/><i> I expected this image to have been at least a top 5. By far this is the most creative entry in this challenge! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>How is reproduction of another''s photograph "creative?" I have absolutely no problem with polishing and advancing the work of another, this is progress (and mycelium''s shot is better than the original.) But of all the adjectives graphicfunk could have used, "original" is one of lesser accuracy.</td>', 'Originally posted by graphicfunk: I expected this image to have been at least a top 5. By far this is the most creative entry in this challenge!   How is reproduction of another''s photograph "creative?" I have absolutely no problem with polishing and advancing the work of another, this is progress (and mycelium''s shot is better than the original.) But of all the adjectives graphicfunk could have used, "original" is one of lesser accuracy.', '2005-08-15 10:28:23.000000', NULL, 0),
